{
  "id": "temporal-motion",
  "title": "Visibility reprojection retains mesh and camera motion on the first edited render and settles on the next",
  "binding": "The existing authored command scheduler submits a slab placement edit at tick 69 and a camera-anchor placement edit at tick 79. They apply on ticks 70 and 80 before those ticks arm captures. The still capture warms display encoding. Every moved region has more than 16 pixels of leftward correspondence, saturating the red motion channel to zero; green remains one half and valid blue is one. The following rendered frame has zero motion and red one half. The discriminating source captures one tick later, so both nonzero motion claims fail while settled claims hold. Schedule manifests and state exports are retained under each run.",
